From bce3375da1b478deabd64fe92a1ac4ac449131b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:49:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Retain the qualified block-sized tile for small transposed
 selections

Upstream-base: a4f0958ce91a5faa99dcc6e329ebcccdbe3c4220.

Rationale: the 128-byte stage changes the generated program and leaves the repeated 96-row BF16 case unqualified. Restore the exact block-sized shared stage that qualified on both v7 boots, while retaining the one-warp dispatch bound. Larger selections continue to use the qualified v6 native-stride program. Every selected GPU program must match its prior qualified CUDA hash and input identity.

Quality: metadata dispatch only combines qualified programs. No new GPU launch, global buffer, dtype/layout materialization, arithmetic order or output-value change. The shared tile follows the normalization block size; the dispatch follows warp size. Tests retain the 31/32/33 boundary and cold startup-freeze coverage.

Tests: exact program-identity validation for all 120 cases on two boots, full numerical/native-layout/graph/startup suite, and expanded IKET probes for both the shared and ordinary paths are required. All rejected variants and observations remain in the experiment.

Upstream-status: local candidate, not submitted upstream.
---
 vllm/v1/worker/gpu/sample/tilelang_logprob.py | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/sample/tilelang_logprob.py b/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/sample/tilelang_logprob.py
index 8d334f8c0e..0fb90ccbe8 100644
--- a/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/sample/tilelang_logprob.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/sample/tilelang_logprob.py
@@ -293,9 +293,9 @@ def topk_log_softmax_kernel(
             T.import_source(_HEADER)
             tx = T.get_thread_binding()
             if prefetch_ids:
-                T.assume(topk <= 32)
+                T.assume(topk <= threads)
                 # Reuse the reduction barriers; each thread later reads its own slot.
-                selected = T.alloc_shared((32,), T.float32)
+                selected = T.alloc_shared((threads,), T.float32)
                 if tx < topk:
                     selected[tx] = T.cast(logits[row, token_ids[row, tx]], T.float32)
             raw = T.alloc_local((per,), logits_dtype)
